From 421bdd1f8fa20cf3ea9be637a1be633795925f00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charliechen114514 <725610365@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 08:27:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/15] hw/input+audio: GT911 touchscreen and WM8960 codec
 models for the AES board
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

GT911 (hw/input/gt911.c): register-level model aligned with the Linux
goodix driver. 16-bit register addressing; ID register answers '911'
(vid 0x0020) so the driver routes to gt911_chip_data (8-byte contacts,
186-byte config). Config page reads zero — checksum fails on purpose,
the same path a fresh chip takes (driver falls back to defaults).
Touch injection from the monitor: gt911_touch x y / gt911_release fill
the FIFO at 0x814e and drive the INT line (wired to GPIO1_IO9); the
guest IRQ handler reads the point over the real I2C path.

WM8960 (hw/audio/wm8960.c): control-plane model at i2c1 0x1a. 7-bit
register + 9-bit data split framing, full read/write-back — the codec
DAPM surface is explorable via i2cdetect/i2cget/i2cset. Audio data
path intentionally not modeled (fsl_sai requires dmaengine PCM; SDMA is
a firmware core a register model cannot honestly fake).

Known issue: the gt911 INT wiring to GPIO1_IO9 does not propagate yet
(gpio_set on the pin works; the model's qemu_irq does not move PSR).
Probe/ID/FIFO/monitor commands verified; E2E 15/15.
